<title>JAPAN: Japan Aug corn imports down 8.47 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Aug corn imports down 8.47 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's August corn imports were down by 8.47 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data issues on Monday showed. Details were as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>			  Aug 96	 July 96	 Aug 95</p>
<p> Total		1,277,819     1,176,165     1,396,142</p>
<p> Feed corn total    744,155	 829,943	 883,196</p>
<p> others		 533,664	 346,222	 512,946</p>
<p>Top supplier of feed corn (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		   717,776	 800,818	 863,294</p>
<p> Argentine	     10,707	  24,039	  19,902</p>
<p> China		    5,227	   5,089	     nil</p>
<p> South Africa	   7,393	     nil	     nil</p>
<p> Australia		3,052	     nil	     nil</p>
<p>Imports in the first eight months of this year totalled 10,497,159 tonnes against 10,972,861 in the same period last year.</p>
</text>
